    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0197" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg127"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 293.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 9, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of June 13, (No. 174,)
                    accompanied by Earl Russell’s final explanation on the case of the Emily St.
                    Pierre, has been received.</p>
                <p>We have been unable here to find the parallel case in the diplomatic
                    correspondence referred to by you in connexion with this subject, and I reserve
                    further remarks upon this case until you shall have been able to send it to us
                    or direct our search for it.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
